uml-nt: lds — collect .lbss into the bss region (OS_WINDOWS)

clang -mcmodel=large emits big bss objects into .lbss; this bss
collector (dyn.lds.S — CONFIG_LD_SCRIPT_DYN=y is the uml_nt build)
names only .dynbss/.bss/COMMON, so .lbss became an ORPHAN section
placed past _end. Every image-end derivation was then wrong by the
whole .lbss extent (~166KB): brk_end = UML_ROUND_UP(&_end) landed
inside live bss (patch 0010), mem_init's memblock_free(brk_end,
uml_reserved - brk_end) handed the buddy allocator the rest of the
live kernel bss — swapper_pg_dir, the D19 anchor words
uml_physmem/high_physmem (0x6043d090/0x6043d0b0), mem_map,
min_low_pfn/max_pfn all included — while the boot memmap survived
only because setup_physmem runs before that free and memblock
allocates top-down.

The S4c2 busybox crash is exactly this: the first order-0-heavy
alloc_pages window (the /bin/busybox exec — bprm mm pgd +
copy_strings argv pages) received the anchor page, the
pagetable/string writes trashed the anchors deterministically
(physmem=0x400000001, high=0x62000200 — twice in a row), and the
next virt_to_page walk (freeing the 131KB read's bio pages)
faulted in kmem_cache_free far from the writer. physmem_size
stayed clean because it lives in a different page — which is why
the crash pointed at ubd, not at the corrupting step. The D19
canary on the os-I/O funnel (5e98421..057ff37) named the first
trashed observation (run 36649012363) and stays as the permanent
tripwire for this class of bug.

Collect .lbss (and .sbss for safety) before __bss_stop/_end so
_end is the real end of loaded memory and the buddy pool starts
above the image.

Signed-off-by: quangdz-comeback <204571370+quangdz-comeback@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 arch/um/kernel/dyn.lds.S | 11 +++++++++++
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/um/kernel/dyn.lds.S b/arch/um/kernel/dyn.lds.S
--- a/arch/um/kernel/dyn.lds.S
+++ b/arch/um/kernel/dyn.lds.S
@@ -166,6 +166,17 @@
    . = ALIGN(32 / 8);
   . = ALIGN(32 / 8);
   }
+#ifdef CONFIG_OS_WINDOWS
+  /* uml-nt: clang emits large-model bss objects into .lbss. This bss
+   * collector does not name it, so .lbss became an orphan section
+   * placed PAST _end — brk_end/uml_reserved then computed off a fake
+   * image end and min_low_pfn admitted LIVE kernel bss (the D19 anchor
+   * words uml_physmem/high_physmem included) to the buddy free pool:
+   * the busybox exec's bprm mm/copy_strings pages trashed them
+   * deterministically (the S4c2 "kmem_cache_free trash"). Collect it —
+   * _end must be the real end of loaded memory. */
+  .lbss : { *(.lbss .lbss.* .sbss .sbss.*) }
+#endif
    __bss_stop = .;
   _end = .;
   PROVIDE (end = .);
